// The sample words for the wireframe deck (docs/redesign/wireframes.html): every screen of all 36 levels.
// These words were written by Claude on the owner's instruction (18 Nov 2026: "don't use open ai for this").
// They are samples for a proposal. They are not the game's final text.
//
// A level:  s    the sentence the child builds. A plain string is a fixed part. A list is a gap:
//                [which button the sample child picks, button, button, button].
//           sol  Florence's solutions: [name, what it is].
//           res  results: [lens id, [rating, words] for each plan]. Ratings: g good, f fair, p poor.
//           again (level 4)  add: one more gap; then new solutions and results.
//           helper (town)  a line that explains Florence.  watch  what the town shows during the tests.  how, lensHow  instructions for this level only.
//           labels  a different name for a check in this level only, by check id.
//           scene  one line shown above the word buttons, so the child knows what the choices are for.
//           retry  { pick, after }  the plan that the sample child tries after pressing Try another plan, and what Florence says about it. Without it, the next plan in the list is used and its results are shown.
//           test  the name of the button that the child presses to start the test (Eco Town, from Astra's feedback). A level with test has no hands step.
//           point  [what Florence asks, what the sample child taps on the town]: the recap in Eco Town, answered by tapping the town.  askF  [a question about Florence, 0 for yes or 1 for no].
//           hands  the short step that the child does by hand.  recap  [question, the right answer, two other answers] shown after the result. The page changes the order of the answers.
//           lens (levels 5 and 6)  the child picks the lenses, so the screen offers the whole town list.
//           reasons, reason (level 6), pick (the plan the sample child chooses), after (what Florence says).
